.TH MORSA 1 "26 July 2026" "Morsa 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
morsa \- Linux metadata, OSINT, evidence correlation, and scoped reconnaissance CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B morsa
.RI [ --project " PATH" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Morsa stores investigations in durable SQLite workspaces, ingests artifacts into a
SHA-256 content-addressable store, extracts bounded metadata, correlates evidence,
discovers public resources, and performs explicitly scoped network operations.
It supports HTTP and SOCKS proxy pools with bounded automatic rotation.
.PP
Commands and machine contracts are English. Human documentation is available in
English and Spanish. JSON and NDJSON objects include a mandatory
.B schema_version
field.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --project " PATH"
Use PATH as the workspace instead of the current directory.
.TP
.B --json
Emit the command's versioned JSON representation. Logs remain on standard error.
.TP
.B --help
Show contextual help.
.SH CORE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI init " [PATH] [--name NAME]"
Create or open a self-contained Morsa workspace.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect SDK/runtime, sandbox helpers, workspace paths, SQLite, and external tools.
.TP
.B version
Print product, protocol, and schema versions.
.TP
.B project status
Summarize project, runs, tasks, artifacts, findings, and pending work.
.TP
.BI scope " add VALUE [--kind KIND] [--max-mode MODE]"
Add an authorized domain, host, URL, address, or CIDR with a maximum activity mode.
.TP
.B scope list
List normalized scope entries.
.SH INGESTION AND PIPELINES
.TP
.BI ingest " file FILE [--max-mb MB]"
Hash and store one local artifact.
.TP
.BI ingest " directory DIRECTORY [--recursive] [--max-files COUNT]"
Ingest a bounded directory set.
.TP
.BI ingest " url URL [--proxy-pool POOL] [--max-mb MB]"
Acquire one in-scope URL and ingest the response artifact.
.TP
.BI discover " documents TARGET [--types TYPES] [--provider PROVIDERS] [--max-results COUNT] [--active-crawl]"
Discover candidate documents with configured providers.
.TP
.BI discover " history TARGET"
Discover historical URLs using Common Crawl.
.TP
.BI discover " import SOURCE [--format FORMAT] [--max-results COUNT]"
Import text, CSV, JSON, NDJSON, HAR, or stdin URL collections.
.TP
.BI fetch " pending [--proxy-pool POOL] [--max-mb MB]"
Acquire pending resources through the bounded network transport.
.TP
.BI run " full TARGET [--types TYPES] [--providers PROVIDERS] [--proxy-pool POOL] [--active-crawl]"
Run discovery, acquisition, analysis, and correlation.
.TP
.BI run " resume [--proxy-pool POOL]"
Resume durable pending work idempotently.
.TP
.B analyze all
Analyze all pending artifacts.
.TP
.B correlate
Create normalized entities and evidence-backed relationships.
.SH RECONNAISSANCE
.TP
.BI recon " dns NAME [--types A,AAAA,MX,NS,SOA,TXT,CNAME,SRV,CAA]"
Resolve selected DNS record types.
.TP
.BI recon " reverse ADDRESSES"
Resolve a comma-separated address set.
.TP
.BI recon " subdomains DOMAIN [--wordlist FILE] [--budget COUNT]"
Enumerate bounded DNS labels with wildcard suppression.
.TP
.BI recon " range CIDR [--budget COUNT]"
Perform bounded PTR enumeration for an authorized prefix.
.TP
.BI recon " axfr ZONE [--server NAME]"
Attempt an explicitly authorized aggressive TCP zone transfer.
.TP
.BI fingerprint " http URL [--proxy-pool POOL]"
Collect bounded HTTP service attributes.
.TP
.BI fingerprint " tls HOST [--port PORT]"
Inspect an in-scope TLS certificate and negotiation.
.TP
.BI fingerprint " banner HOST [--port PORT] [--protocol tcp]"
Collect a bounded service banner.
.TP
.BI web " crawl URL [--depth DEPTH] [--max-pages COUNT] [--proxy-pool POOL]"
Create a bounded same-host HTTP map.
.TP
.BI web " backups URL [--budget COUNT] [--proxy-pool POOL]"
Validate evidence-derived backup candidates in aggressive mode.
.TP
.BI malware " scan [--artifact ID]"
Run local static risk checks and optional ClamAV integration.
.TP
.BI malware " yara RULES [--artifact ID]"
Run an installed YARA engine against stored artifacts.
.SH PROXIES
.TP
.BI proxy " pool add NAME [--policy POLICY] [--max-rotations COUNT] [--max-attempts COUNT] [--allow-direct-fallback]"
Create or update a proxy pool.
.TP
.B proxy pool list
List pools and policies.
.TP
.BI proxy " import SOURCE [--pool NAME]"
Import user-managed endpoints from a supported source.
.TP
.BI proxy " source list"
List supported source adapters and environment availability without exposing values.
.TP
.BI proxy " source load SOURCE [--pool NAME]"
Load a file, stdin, environment, HTTPS, command, or inline source into a pool.
.TP
.BI proxy " status [--pool NAME]"
Show health, counters, latency, and cooldown state.
.TP
.BI proxy " reset [--pool NAME]"
Reset transient health for a pool.
.TP
.BI proxy " test POOL [--url URL]"
Validate rotation and connectivity against an HTTPS target.
.PP
Policies are
.BR sticky ,
.BR round-robin ,
.BR random ,
.BR weighted ,
.BR least-latency ,
and
.BR failover .
Supported transports are HTTP forward, HTTPS CONNECT, SOCKS4, SOCKS5, and
SOCKS5h. Credentials use secret references and are redacted from persistence.
.SH PLUGINS, REPORTS, AND MCP
.TP
.BI plugin " install SOURCE [--no-activate]"
Install a directory or ZIP containing morsa-plugin.json.
.TP
.BI plugin " inspect ID"
Inspect all installed versions and manifest validation.
.TP
.BI plugin " update SOURCE [--no-activate]"
Install and normally activate a newer package version.
.TP
.BI plugin " activate ID VERSION"
Atomically select one installed version.
.TP
.BI plugin " rollback ID"
Select the previous valid version.
.TP
.BI plugin " remove ID [--version VERSION]"
Remove one or all versions.
.TP
.BI plugin " run ID OPERATION [--input JSON] [--timeout SECONDS]"
Invoke the morsa-plugin/1 JSONL process contract.
.TP
.BI report " json|html|csv [--output FILE] [--include-sensitive]"
Write a versioned report. Sensitive values are pseudonymized by default.
.TP
.BI report " bundle [--output FILE] [--redact] [--include-sensitive]"
Create a reproducible evidence bundle; redacted bundles omit artifact payloads.
.TP
.BI graph " export [--format graphml|gexf|dot|csv] [--output FILE]"
Export the correlation graph.
.PP
The MCP server is the separately installed
.B morsa-mcp
helper under libexec. It transports MCP exclusively over standard input/output;
diagnostic logs are written only to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I morsa.toml
Project configuration. The XDG user fallback is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/morsa/config.toml .
Network rate/timeout/query budgets, artifact budgets/sandbox, security redaction,
private-network policy, and proxy profiles are validated and applied at startup.
.TP
.I morsa.db
SQLite workspace database. WAL sidecars can exist while Morsa is running.
.TP
.I artifacts/
SHA-256 content-addressable artifact store.
.TP
.I .morsa/plugins/
Versioned plugin catalog and active-version pointers.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR HTTP_PROXY , " " HTTPS_PROXY , " " ALL_PROXY , " " NO_PROXY
Standard proxy selection variables. NO_PROXY always takes precedence for matching
destinations.
.TP
.B MORSA_SEARXNG_URL
Base URL for an explicitly configured SearXNG provider.
.TP
.B MORSA_PARSER_HOST
Path to the parser host executable in nonstandard installations.
.TP
.B MORSA_PLUGIN_HOST
Path to the plugin host executable in nonstandard installations.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME , " " XDG_STATE_HOME , " " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Override Linux configuration, state, and cache roots.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 3
Policy, scope, or bounded-input rejection used by active commands.
.TP
.B 5
Partial completion with persisted diagnostics.
.TP
.B 7
Cooperative cancellation.
.TP
.B 8
An installed plugin version failed catalog validation.
.TP
.B 9
Plugin runtime or host failure.
.TP
.B 10
Doctor or database health gate failure.
.PP
Other failures return nonzero. Machine clients should inspect the JSON error code.
.SH SECURITY
Network operations are rejected unless allowed by workspace scope. Redirects are
revalidated. Proxy authentication, cookies, and handlers are isolated by identity.
No direct fallback is silent. Parser and plugin boundaries are separate processes.
